%% @kicker Flat scan vs HNSW
%% @alt A query vector can be answered two ways. A flat scan compares the query with every stored vector, so its work grows with the number of vectors. An HNSW graph index navigates sparse long-distance links first and compares only a small set of candidate vectors near the answer.
